# Dotfiles Workflow Improvements

## Current Stack Summary

**Core:** zsh + zinit → starship → ghostty → aerospace + sketchybar → tmux  
**Editors:** nvim (minimal), IntelliJ (heavy IdeaVim), VSCode, Zed  
**Dev:** Java/jenv/maven, JS/bun/node, Docker/colima, K8s, AWS  
**AI:** opencode, claude, gemini, supermaven  
**Productivity:** Trello→Day One pipeline, timers, Raycast, Heynote, OBS recording  

---

## 1. Setup / Maintainability

- `setup.sh` mixes `stow` + manual `ln -s` → brittle, not idempotent
- Missing `Brewfile.lock.json` handling
- No `.env` template for Trello API keys / secrets
- Scripts have hardcoded paths, inconsistent shebangs
- No uninstall/restore script

**Quick wins:**
- [ ] Replace manual `ln -s` with `stow` or a single symlink loop
- [ ] Add guard clauses (check if symlink already exists)
- [ ] Create `.env.example` for secrets
- [ ] Standardize all scripts to `#!/usr/bin/env bash` with `set -euo pipefail`

---

## 2. Project Context Switching (Critical for Freelancer)

- **No direnv** → can't auto-load per-client env vars, Java versions, API keys
- **No sesh config** despite installing it → missing tmux session wizard
- **No project switcher** → jumping between client repos is manual
- jenv is loaded every shell but no per-project `.java-version` workflow

**Quick wins:**
- [ ] Install & configure `direnv` with `.envrc` templates
- [ ] Configure `sesh` with project bindings (`sesh connect`)
- [ ] Add `zoxide` integration for project directories
- [ ] Create `.java-version` + `.nvmrc` auto-switch aliases

**Deeper impact:**
- [ ] Tmuxinator/sesh project templates per client (frontend/backend/infra)
- [ ] Single `work` command: `work <client>` → cd + tmux session + direnv + ide

---

## 3. Shell Performance

- 5+ `eval "$(...)"` on every shell startup (starship, jenv, fzf, zoxide, carapace)
- No lazy loading → shell starts slow
- Missing **atuin** (synced shell history)

**Quick wins:**
- [ ] Lazy-load jenv via function wrapper (only on `java`/`mvn` call)
- [ ] Lazy-load carapace completions
- [ ] Install atuin + bind to Ctrl-R

**Deeper impact:**
- [ ] Profile shell startup (`zsh -xv` or `zsh-startup-timer`)
- [ ] Move heavy inits to background or defer

---

## 4. Neovim — Too Minimal for Client Work

- No LSP, no treesitter highlighting, no diagnostics, no formatting
- No git integration (fugitive/gitsigns)
- Only telescope + supermaven

**Quick wins:**
- [ ] Add treesitter for syntax highlighting
- [ ] Add LSP config (lsp-zero or nvim-lspconfig) for Java/TS
- [ ] Add conform.nvim for formatting

**Deeper impact:**
- [ ] Evaluate LazyVim vs maintaining own config
- [ ] Add gitsigns + diffview for git workflow
- [ ] Add harpoon for file navigation
- [ ] Add which-key for discoverability

---

## 5. Git Workflow

- `gpp` does `pull; push` blindly
- No conventional commits helper
- No branch naming convention enforcement
- No PR/draft creation helpers
- `gh-dash` installed but no custom config

**Quick wins:**
- [ ] Replace `gpp` with `gpl && gps` (fail on pull conflict)
- [ ] Add `gc` helper for conventional commits (`gc feat "msg"`)
- [ ] Add branch naming alias: `gbf` → `git checkout -b feat/TICKET-desc`

**Deeper impact:**
- [ ] gh-dash config with custom sections (drafts, review requested)
- [ ] Pre-commit hooks for lint/format
- [ ] Git worktree aliases for parallel PRs

